`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"Deduplication and idempotency"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Before filing, the importer loads existing open GitHub issues (best-effort; proceeds without dedup if GitHub is unavailable). For each anomaly it computes a dedup key from ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"(anomaly_class, command_prefix, reporter_channel)"})," and derives a deterministic ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"observer-dedup:<8-char-hex>"})," label. If an open issue already carries that label, the anomaly is ",e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"folded"})," (appended as a thread message) instead of filed as a new issue."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Within a single batch, the first occurrence of a dedup key is filed and subsequent occurrences fold into the just-filed issue — so running the same log twice does not create duplicates."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"PII redaction"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Before any issue is filed or folded, the title and body pass through the same ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"runRedactionGuard"})," backstop used by ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"issues create"}),". UUIDs, email addresses, auth tokens, and home-directory paths are replaced with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"<LABEL:hash>"})," placeholders. Lines are never dropped for containing PII; if the redaction guard itself throws (a programming error), the line is counted as ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"issues_skipped"})," in the sweep report."]}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h3,{children:"Reporter environment requirement"}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["A reporter environment field (",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"reporter_git_sha"})," or ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"reporter_app_version"}),") must be resolvable for each anomaly. Resolution order: per-line JSONL field → ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--reporter-git-sha"})," / ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--reporter-app-version"})," CLI flag → CLI binary version from ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"package.json"}),". If none of these are available (common in dev builds), the import fails fast with an actionable error before making any network calls."]}),`
